<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>GR-008 Turbine Plane</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.7">model.sdf</sdf>
  <author>
    <name>tootiredtoo</name>
    <email>oschest@gmail.com</email>
  </author>
  <description>
    Approximate Gazebo Classic model for a 1 m turbine fixed-wing aircraft
    (Swiwin SW80, rear-mounted, ~80 N max thrust).  Intended for ArduPilot SITL
    with the catapult_ground_hold state machine.

    Airframe summary:
      Wingspan : 1.0 m    Length   : 1.0 m
      AUW      : 3.5 kg   CG       : 0.38 m from nose
      Turbine  : SW80, rear-mounted (140 000 RPM cruise / 156 000 RPM max)
      FC       : Pixhawk 6X
      Sensors  : GPS, INS, pitot (nose-left)

    Catapult scenario:
      Rail angle : 12.3 deg nose-up
      Launch     : manual — pilot spools turbine to cruise RPM then fires
      No electronic sync between catapult trigger and autopilot.

    Servo assignments (ArduPilot SERVO functions):
      SERVO1 (ch 0) = aileron left   (function  4)
      SERVO2 (ch 1) = aileron right  (function  4, reversed)
      SERVO3 (ch 2) = throttle       (function 70)
      SERVO4 (ch 3) = elevator       (function 19)
      SERVO5 (ch 4) = rudder         (function 21)

    All aerodynamic coefficients are first-order approximations.
    Run autotune / TECS tune before using for quantitative flight analysis.
  </description>
</model>
